WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.420
Consider an agent used by a small
business.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.658
The agent is asked to summarize
yesterday's failed payments.

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:14.007
The agent uses external tools such as APIs
or MCPs to fetch

00:00:14.087 --> 00:00:17.927
failed payments, identify the affected
accounts, and retrieve

00:00:18.007 --> 00:00:19.687
relevant support tickets.

00:00:20.007 --> 00:00:23.007
Each result returns to the model before it
can choose the

00:00:23.047 --> 00:00:24.247
next request.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:28.193
That adds inference work and makes the
next request wait.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.340
In this sequence, three requests and a
final interpretation

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.299
take four model rounds.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.618
Instead of sequential tool calling,

00:00:38.618 --> 00:00:42.422
the model may write a program that calls
the three tools.

00:00:42.422 --> 00:00:45.586
Inside the program, it totals the failed
payments,

00:00:45.586 --> 00:00:47.774
identifies the impacted accounts,

00:00:47.774 --> 00:00:50.294
and links them to three support tickets -

00:00:50.294 --> 00:00:52.012
without another model round.

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:55.893
The program returns the final report.

00:00:56.213 --> 00:00:59.893
The model provides the requested summary,
financial impact,

00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:03.253
and customer list while keeping raw
records separate from

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:04.723
the primary output.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:09.713
The process is reduced from four model
rounds to two.

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:14.193
Routine work runs as code, maintaining a
smaller, more focused

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:15.829
conversation context.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:20.733
Anthropic demonstrated that code execution
dramatically

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.253
lowers context use.

00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:26.333
CodeAct improved task success rate
meaningfully by having

00:01:26.413 --> 00:01:29.453
agents write programs instead of calling
tools.

00:01:29.693 --> 00:01:33.773
Cloudflare's code mode showed roughly a
1000 x reduction

00:01:33.853 --> 00:01:38.173
in tool-interface tokens by serving API
documentation instead

00:01:38.213 --> 00:01:39.613
of tool schemas.

00:01:39.693 --> 00:01:43.213
These results help explain why code
execution is becoming

00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:46.653
an integral part of the agent stack, and
is expected to

00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:48.376
only grow in the future.
